// EXPECT-ERROR: value -1 does not fit in u16 - write u16(-1) if the truncation is deliberate
// The return slot is assigned like anything else, so checkAssignable guards it.
// -1 is used rather than something like 70000, which never reaches here: a
// literal outside 16 bits is rejected earlier, when the literal itself is
// resolved. This is also the negative-into-unsigned case, which used to become
// 65535 in silence.
u16 big() {
  return -1
}

u16 out
out = big()
